# The reader example's scripted session (gates/reader.sh) over a feed of 3,000 articles: no Rust twin;
# the images are looked at by eye. Window coordinates (the images are twice the size): the toolbar's
# icon buttons at y 24, reload 24, previous 60, next 96, star 132, close 168, theme 940, settings 976;
# the search box 150,73; the list's rows (with summaries) y = 157, 225, 293, 361, ...; the first tab
# 388,65. In the settings dialog: the font slider's thumb 396,147 on a track from x 293 to 707, the
# theme select 550,191 (its "Dark" 550,263), the order select 550,239, the switch 311,281.
# The offscreen clock moves only with `advance` (toasts slide in, the article fades in).
size 1000 660
frame
sleep 300
frame
advance 500
shot 01-loaded.png
# a tooltip on an icon button
move 24 24
advance 1500
shot 02-tooltip.png
# an article opens in a tab and fades in over 200 ms
click 150 225
advance 60
shot 03-fading.png
advance 300
shot 04-open.png
# a second article, a second tab; star it
click 150 361
advance 300
click 132 24
advance 300
shot 05-starred.png
# back to the first tab; alt-down opens the next article in the list
click 388 65
advance 300
shot 06-first-tab.png
key alt-down
advance 300
shot 07-next.png
# far down the list
scroll 150 600 -60000
frame
frame
shot 08-scrolled.png
# a search
click 150 73
type bread
advance 100
shot 09-search.png
key ctrl-a
key backspace
advance 100
# the settings: font size 18, no summaries, the dark theme
key ctrl-,
advance 300
shot 10-settings.png
drag 396 147 500 147
advance 300
click 311 281
advance 300
click 550 191
advance 300
shot 11-theme-select.png
click 550 263
advance 300
shot 12-dark.png
key escape
advance 300
shot 13-dark-closed.png
# ctrl-w closes the tab; ctrl-r loads the feed again on the thread: a second toast
key ctrl-w
advance 300
shot 14-tab-closed.png
key ctrl-r
sleep 300
frame
advance 500
shot 15-reloaded.png
